The changes I made:

1. Added missing required properties to the app object:
   - `categories`: Array with at least one category
   - `enabled`: Boolean flag
   - `isInstalled`: Boolean flag
   - `isSetupAlready`: Boolean flag
   - `variant`: String value
   - `type`: String value

2. Updated the context value to include:
   - `LockedIcon`: Set to null as it's optional
   - Updated `getAppData` to return an object with `enabled` property

These changes should resolve the "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading '0')" error, which was occurring because the app object didn't have the `categories` array that AppCard was trying to access.

The error was specifically happening at this line in AppCard.tsx:
```javascript
app?.categories[0].charAt(0).toUpperCase() + app?.categories[0].slice(1)
```

Now that we've provided the `categories` array with at least one item, this should work correctly.

